# tools/l/line_length_gate_witness.rish -- 80-column gate for Glow,
# ratchet for all others
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/line_length_gate_witness.rish
#
# WHAT THIS GUARDS. The 80-column standard seated `20261104` on
# Keaton's word, departing from TigerBeetle's 100 toward Urbit's elder
# discipline for accessibility. Glow is gated at zero overlong lines
# from that stamp. Every other TAME family ratchets under a ceiling
# that only falls.
#
# Purely local -- no key, no network, no funds, no device.

say "line-length-gate: 80-column gate for Glow, ratchet for others."
say "line-length-gate: Seated 20261104 on Keaton's word."

# the field
let field = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/l/line_length_gate_scan.sh" "--list"]
say field.out
say field.err

# reach -- a walk that found nothing reports a perfect zero
assert field.ok else "line-length-gate: the scan refused -- read verdict= above"
assert (field.out contains "total_files=0") == false else "line-length-gate: the walk read no source at all"

# the gate: Glow at zero overlong lines
assert field.out contains "glow_over=0" else "line-length-gate: Glow carries lines past 80 columns -- fix them before this lands"
assert field.out contains "glow_verdict=ok" else "line-length-gate: Glow gate RED"

# the ratchet: others under ceiling (reported, not gated yet --
# the population is too large for a gate that reds on ordinary work)
# When the ratchet is low enough to gate, change this to an assert.

say "GREEN: line-length-gate -- Glow holds at 80 columns."
